The `ToUpperMiddleware` that will `ToUpper` each `TextMessageUpdate`.  It does not support the `TextMessage` because, in this example, one of the following reasons could be used to explain why.  
* the cost of performing the middleware logic is expensive (cpu, memory, resource) and performing it once.
* the developer didn't know it should be handled
* the end user is not handling the `TextMessage` from the stream.

```
    public class ToUpperMiddleware : IStreamingMiddleware
    {
        public string? Name => nameof(ToUpperMiddleware);

        public async IAsyncEnumerable<IMessage> InvokeAsync(MiddlewareContext context, IStreamingAgent agent, [EnumeratorCancellation] CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)
        {
            // streaming middleware input, (maniuplate the input messages)

            // the transition from the input to the output happens when the reply is created

            // streaming middleware output (manipulate the output messages)
            var streamingReply = agent.GenerateStreamingReplyAsync(context.Messages, context.Options, cancellationToken);

            await foreach (var message in streamingReply)
            {
                if (message is TextMessageUpdate textMessage)
                {
                    textMessage.Content = textMessage.Content?.ToUpper();
                }
                yield return message;
            }
        }

        public Task<IMessage> InvokeAsync(MiddlewareContext context, IAgent agent, CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)
        {
            throw new NotImplementedException();
        }
    }
```

