**Solution for GitHub Issue #4373: Setting up Full TLS between all nodes**

**Why is this solution needed?**
--------------------------------

To make it easier to take workloads to production, we need to provide documentation on how to set up end-to-end TLS between all nodes. This will ensure secure communication between nodes and provide a secure environment for production workloads.

**Solution Overview**
-------------------

To set up full TLS between all nodes, we will use Azure Bicep to deploy a sample infrastructure with TLS enabled. We will also provide instructions on how to configure the TLS certificates and keys.

**Prerequisites**
-----------------

* Azure subscription
* Azure CLI installed
* Azure Bicep installed
* A domain name (e.g., example.com)

**Step 1: Create a new Azure Bicep file**
--------------------------------------

Create a new file called `main.bicep` with the following content:
```bicep
// main.bicep

// Define variables
param location string = resourceGroup().location
param domainName string = 'example.com'

// Define resources
